# TrackX .gitignore
#
# Added in the Phase 10 security audit: this repo had NO .gitignore at all
# before this. That's a real risk ahead of Phase 14 (public deployment) -
# once a real .env with a real SECRET_KEY/DB password/API key exists for
# deploying this, there was nothing stopping it from being committed by
# accident. This does not change anything about what's currently tracked;
# it only prevents future accidents.

# Environment / secrets - never commit real credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# SQLite databases (demo/dev data, regenerated by demo/seed_demo_data.py)
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Node / frontend build output
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
node_modules/

# Uploaded/generated media (video uploads, plate crops, run outputs)
outputs/
backend/app/media/
**/video_uploads/
**/plate_crops/

# Model weights (large binaries - track via release assets / Git LFS instead
# of the repo history if they need to be versioned)
*.pt
!yolov8n.pt

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
